  "Package": "MsBackendParquet",
  "Title": "Apache Parquet-based Mass Spectrometry Data Backend",
  "Version": "0.99.10",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\n\"Ossama\",\n\"Edbali\",\nrole=c(\"aut\",\"cre\"),\nemail=\"o.edbali@bham.ac.uk\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0003-0132-8668\")),\nperson(\nc(\"Ralf\",\"Johannes\", \"Maria\"),\n\"Weber\",\nrole=c(\"aut\"),\nemail=\"r.j.weber@bham.ac.uk\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-8796-4771\")),\nperson(\n\"Johannes\",\n\"Rainer\",\nrole=c(\"ctb\"),\nemail=\"Johannes.Rainer@eurac.edu\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-6977-7147\")),\nperson(\n\"BioFAIR UK\",\nrole=\"fnd\",\ncomment=\"BioFAIR Pathfinder Project\"))",
  "Description": "Mass spectrometry (MS) data backend for the Spectra\nBioconductor package that stores and retrieves spectra and peak\ndata from on-disk Apache Parquet datasets. Spectra metadata\ntogether with m/z and intensity values are stored in a columnar\nParquet format that supports compression, dictionary encoding\nand Hive-style partitioning. Datasets are written with the\nApache Arrow R bindings and queried with DuckDB. Spectra\nvariables are held in a bounded in-memory index so that\nfiltering and metadata access are fast while peak data remains\non disk.",
